From: Wendy Labs <engineering@wendy.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: preserve legacy advertising across central connects

A central connection can complete while legacy advertising is enabled.
Clearing HCI_LE_ADV then makes hci_disable_advertising_sync skip the actual
controller disable. Legacy advertisement rotation repeatedly programs
parameters on the still-enabled controller and receives Command Disallowed.
Preserve the flag for central and failed legacy completions so the next
parameter update explicitly disables advertising first. Keep successful
peripheral termination and existing extended-advertising behavior unchanged.

Observed with BCM43455: successful central completion followed by repeated
0x2006/0x0c responses, while peers continue receiving advertisements.

Upstream-Status: Pending [successful-central legacy variant]
Signed-off-by: Wendy Labs <engineering@wendy.dev>
---
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
@@ -5654,10 +5654,15 @@
 
 	hci_dev_lock(hdev);
 
-	/* All controllers implicitly stop advertising in the event of a
-	 * connection, so ensure that the state bit is cleared.
+	/* A legacy advertiser stops when it accepts a peripheral connection.
+	 * An outgoing central connection does not terminate advertising, which
+	 * may have been enabled while the connection was pending. Keep the
+	 * flag on failed attempts too: a later restart must explicitly disable
+	 * advertising before changing its parameters. Preserve the existing
+	 * extended-advertising bookkeeping here.
 	 */
-	hci_dev_clear_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_ADV);
+	if (ext_adv_capable(hdev) || (!status && role == HCI_ROLE_SLAVE))
+		hci_dev_clear_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_ADV);
 
 	/* Check for existing connection:
 	 *
